       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg in one dose is well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg. That raises the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- Another dose, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you've confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it now."
