       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose twice the labeled maximum. At 5,100 mg/day, the risks are real: lactic acidosis, severe GI toxicity, and hypoglycemia when combined with other agents. Normal kidney and liver function lowers those risks but doesn't remove them.\n\nI can enter any of these now:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum).\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day).\n- **A lower starting dose with titration**, such as 500 mg twice daily, increasing over 1\u20132 weeks. This is often better tolerated.\n\nIf you think this patient needs an off-label dose, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy first. I can also enter the order with a note saying it's pending pharmacy review.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
      }
